/*!
    \struct IndexSerializationContext
    \internal
    \brief Supplies publication locations and policy to the index section serializer.

    The caller owns this context for the duration of serialization. Index
    export and WebXML supply separate contexts; the serializer does not choose
    a generator or derive an href from an output extension. Caller-provided
    locations may still come from a legacy generator during migration.
*/

/*!
    \enum IndexSerializationContext::ExampleEntries
    \internal

    Controls whether example file and image entries appear inside their
    example section.

    \value Inline Write nested entries and resolve their hrefs through
                  exampleFileLocation.
    \value Separate Omit nested entries; the caller writes them separately.
*/

/*!
    \variable IndexSerializationContext::documentLocation
    Returns the complete href for a document node, including its fragment.
    The serializer writes the href without changing its path or fragment.
    This callback must remain valid throughout serialization.
*/

/*!
    \variable IndexSerializationContext::exampleFileLocation
    Returns a complete href for an example file or image. Required when
    exampleEntries is Inline and an example contains files or images.
    This callback must remain valid throughout serialization.
*/

/*!
    \variable IndexSerializationContext::inclusionPolicy
    Filters serialized nodes and functions independently of the renderer.
*/

/*!
    \variable IndexSerializationContext::project
    The project name written to the INDEX element. WebXML sections do not
    use this value.
*/

/*!
    \variable IndexSerializationContext::exampleEntries
    Selects whether example files and images are nested in the section or
    written separately by the caller.
*/

/*!
    \variable IndexSerializationContext::storeLocationInfo
    Includes declaration file paths and line numbers when available.
*/
